
 PHASE 3: Testing & Uploading Code to Production


💻 Step 3.1: On Your Laptop

1. Click your folder's top address bar window, type cmd, and press Enter to launch your terminal.
2. Install the modules onto your laptop by typing:
pip install opencv-python numpy pyttsx3

pip install opencv-python numpy pyttsx3
python src/main.py
1. Verify your camera stream window opens and speaks when objects are shown. Press q to close it down.

🌐 Step 3.2: On GitHub

1. On your repository home page, click Add file -> Upload files.
2. Drag and drop your src folder (main.py, detector.py, text_to_speech.py) directly from your desktop into the web browser dashboard window.
3. Note: Do not upload the large .weights file, as GitHub blocks files over 100MB.
4. Type Upload application source code files in the commit description box at the bottom and click Commit changes.

